  "worked_solution": "Remember that the sum of the interior angles of a polygon with $n$ sides is ${180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2).$\n\nTo find the number of sides in our polygon, we start by setting up the following equation:\n\n$$\n{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)={360}^{∘}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $n,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2) & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ n-2 & =\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{{180}^{∘}} \\\\ n-2 & =2 \\\\ n & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polygon has $n=4$ sides (so it is a quadrilateral).",
